 dialogue:{title:"Una carta de recomendación", scene:"Mariana, jefa de recursos humanos, revisa con su colega Graham una carta de recomendación que él escribió para un exempleado.", a:"Mariana", b:"Graham", lines:[
  ["A","Graham, I've read your reference for Daniel. Can I be candid with you?","Graham, leí tu carta de referencia para Daniel. ¿Puedo ser franca contigo?"],
  ["B","Of course. Is something wrong with it?","Claro. ¿Tiene algo malo?"],
  ["A","Not wrong exactly, but some of your word choices send the wrong signal. You describe him as 'pushy with clients'.","No exactamente malo, pero algunas palabras que elegiste mandan la señal equivocada. Lo describes como 'insistente con los clientes'."],
  ["B","I meant it as a compliment. He never takes no for an answer.","Lo dije como elogio. Nunca acepta un no por respuesta."],
  ["A","Then you mean assertive. 'Pushy' suggests he bulldozes people; 'assertive' suggests he stands his ground politely.","Entonces quieres decir firme. 'Pushy' sugiere que atropella a la gente; 'assertive' sugiere que se hace valer con cortesía."],
  ["B","Fair point. What else?","Buen punto. ¿Qué más?"],
  ["A","You say he was 'stingy with the department's budget'. A recruiter will read that as mean-spirited.","Dices que era 'tacaño con el presupuesto del departamento'. Un reclutador lo leerá como mezquino."],
  ["B","Whereas 'thrifty' would sound prudent, I suppose.","Mientras que 'ahorrativo' sonaría prudente, supongo."],
  ["A","Exactly. Or 'cost-conscious', if you want something more corporate.","Exacto. O 'consciente de los costos', si quieres algo más corporativo."],
  ["B","I also wrote that he's 'inquisitive'. Is that all right?","También escribí que es 'inquisitivo'. ¿Eso está bien?"],
  ["A","That one's perfect. Just don't change it to 'nosy', or he'll never work again.","Esa es perfecta. Solo no la cambies por 'metiche', o no vuelve a conseguir trabajo."],
  ["B","Ha! And 'stubborn'? I said he was stubborn about quality.","¡Ja! ¿Y 'terco'? Dije que era terco con la calidad."],
  ["A","Try 'steadfast' or 'uncompromising about quality'. Same fact, far kinder connotation.","Prueba 'firme' o 'intransigente con la calidad'. El mismo hecho, una connotación mucho más amable."],
  ["B","It's Russell's emotional conjugation, isn't it? I'm firm, you're obstinate, he's pig-headed.","Es la conjugación emocional de Russell, ¿no? Yo soy firme, tú eres obstinado, él es terco como una mula."],
  ["A","Precisely. In a reference, every adjective is a verdict.","Precisamente. En una referencia, cada adjetivo es un veredicto."],
  ["B","I'll redraft it tonight. Thanks for not being smug about it.","La reescribo esta noche. Gracias por no ser engreída al respecto."]
 ]},
